  "narrative": {
    "intro": "RTX has $4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. RTX recorded 822 awards so far, with an average award size of $4.8M, and obligations are down 45.6% year over year. The Department of Defense provided $4B in obligations, making the Department of Defense the dominant federal buyer. Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing is the largest market by obligation at $1.7B, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $819M and Aircraft Manufacturing at $805M. Other Support Activities for Air Transportation accounted for $552M, while Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $42.9M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounted for $14.1M. Historical obligations show variation: FY21 was $3.7B, FY22 was $8B, FY23 was $8.2B, FY24 was $5B, and FY25 was $7.3B. Smaller federal buyers in FY2026 to date include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $1.2M and the Department of Homeland Security at $233K. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove RTX's federal obligations this year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense drove RTX's federal obligations with $4B in FY2026 to date. Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing contributed $1.7B, and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing added $819M. Aircraft Manufacturing contributed $805M, and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation contributed $552M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are RTX's federal sales across agencies and markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense accounts for the majority of RTX's FY2026 to date obligations at $4B. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration accounted for $1.2M and the Department of Homeland Security accounted for $233K. Market concentration is concentrated in aerospace-related NAICS, led by Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing at $1.7B and three other aircraft-related markets with obligations of $819M, $805M, and $552M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
